by giving you a
couple of clicks.

00:43:05.810 --> 00:43:07.780
So right from within
the Informatica UI,

00:43:07.780 --> 00:43:10.060
you can push these
business processes

00:43:10.060 --> 00:43:13.930
as secure, managed API proxies.

00:43:13.930 --> 00:43:17.530
And they can then be automated
into the API lifecycle,

00:43:17.530 --> 00:43:21.880
so you can very confidently
share that with mobile apps,

00:43:21.880 --> 00:43:23.410
with any other
connected experience

00:43:23.410 --> 00:43:25.210
that you're trying to deliver.

00:43:25.210 --> 00:43:28.210
The second thing that
we looked at was,

00:43:28.210 --> 00:43:31.450
without leaving the
Apigee user interface,

00:43:31.450 --> 00:43:34.720
API developers were interacting
with these kind of very

00:43:34.720 --> 00:43:39.297
critical processes, can simply
use the extensions framework

00:43:39.297 --> 00:43:40.880
and the first of the
extension that we

00:43:40.880 --> 00:43:43.810
have built to the
Informatica Integration Cloud

00:43:43.810 --> 00:43:46.110
and integrate with
those processes,

00:43:46.110 --> 00:43:49.270
turn them into APIs
very, very rapidly.

00:43:49.270 --> 00:43:52.570
And the last announcement that
Pratik took us through today

00:43:52.570 --> 00:43:56.380
was that we are going to use
the exact same extensions

00:43:56.380 --> 00:43:59.950
framework, which we have
used to enable the nine

00:43:59.950 --> 00:44:04.210
extensions that you
saw today, and take

00:44:04.210 --> 00:44:08.390
the rich palette of connectors
that Informatica has

00:44:08.390 --> 00:44:12.160
to a variety of different
kinds of data sources,

00:44:12.160 --> 00:44:14.350
all the way from
SaaS applications,

00:44:14.350 --> 00:44:16.930
big data systems,
mainframes, and a bunch

00:44:16.930 --> 00:44:20.740
of different on-premise sources
and turn them into connectors,

00:44:20.740 --> 00:44:24.430
which customers can use directly
from within the Apigee user

00:44:24.430 --> 00:44:25.250
interface.

00:44:25.250 --> 00:44:30.010
We believe that tackles a set
of use cases for API developers

00:44:30.010 --> 00:44:32.050
when they are not really
interested in building

00:44:32.050 --> 00:44:34.330
